    "body": "### Why\n[AutoCorrect](https://github.com/huacnlee/autocorrect) checks and fixes spacing, punctuation, and spelling between CJK and English text, in Markdown, plain text, and the strings and comments of source files. It has 1.6k GitHub stars, a Homebrew formula (`brew install autocorrect`), and editor plugins for VS Code, IntelliJ, and Zed. Its language server is built in and starts with `autocorrect server`.\n\n### What\nAdd `lsp/autocorrect.lua`, so users can enable it with `vim.lsp.enable('autocorrect')`.\n\n### Notes\n- `.autocorrectrc` comes before `.git` in `root_markers`. The server reads `.autocorrectrc` and `.autocorrectignore` only from the root directory ([`reload_config`](https://github.com/huacnlee/autocorrect/blob/e1a75da3faa9b1f005db97b77f47eb67abe1395e/autocorrect-lsp/src/lib.rs#L191-L205)). With `.git` first, a `.autocorrectrc` in a subdirectory of a repository has no effect.\n- `filetypes` is not set, as in `typos_lsp`. The server picks the format from the file path ([`lint_for(input, path)`](https://github.com/huacnlee/autocorrect/blob/e1a75da3faa9b1f005db97b77f47eb67abe1395e/autocorrect-lsp/src/lib.rs#L85)), and its Zed extension enables it for about 20 languages, including plain text.\n- The server works on a single file with no root, so `workspace_required` is not set.\n- Tested with Nvim 0.12.5 and autocorrect 2.16.3 on macOS: diagnostics in Markdown, a Lua comment, and a `.txt` file; the \"AutoCorrect Fix\" code action; a rule turned off in `.autocorrectrc` and a file in `.autocorrectignore` are respected in a subdirectory root.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-30T10:28:24Z",
